{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page": "s-shared-semantics",
      "audio": "audio/1.wav",
      "duration": 154.92,
      "method": "sentences",
      "speech": [
        0.216,
        154.428
      ],
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "These days, almost everyone works with an AI assistant.",
          "start": 0.216,
          "end": 3.322
        },
        {
          "text": "It helps us write code and find answers faster.",
          "start": 4.514,
          "end": 7.51
        },
        {
          "text": "But each of us uses it in our own way, and what one person learns stays with that person.",
          "start": 8.873,
          "end": 14.718
        },
        {
          "text": "So working as a team takes more care than before.",
          "start": 16.119,
          "end": 18.813
        },
        {
          "text": "If a team wants to work with AI together, there are five things worth sharing.",
          "start": 20.011,
          "end": 24.253
        },
        {
          "text": "The first one is the workflow: the way the work moves.",
          "start": 26.553,
          "end": 29.625
        },
        {
          "text": "You say what you need, in your own words, to one agent: the orchestrator.",
          "start": 30.933,
          "end": 34.571
        },
        {
          "text": "It turns that into clear steps, and hands each step to the agent that knows that area best.",
          "start": 35.931,
          "end": 41.942
        },
        {
          "text": "Every one of those agents is built in the same way,",
          "start": 43.279,
          "end": 46.214
        },
        {
          "text": "and they all report back in the same form.",
          "start": 47.211,
          "end": 49.194
        },
        {
          "text": "Around them, a few fixed rules in code make sure nothing goes off course.",
          "start": 50.508,
          "end": 54.642
        },
        {
          "text": "The second thing to share is standards.",
          "start": 56.797,
          "end": 59.082
        },
        {
          "text": "When everyone follows the same patterns, the work comes out the same, no matter who asked for it.",
          "start": 60.219,
          "end": 65.489
        },
        {
          "text": "The results are structured, so the next agent can pick them up right away,",
          "start": 66.914,
          "end": 70.994
        },
        {
          "text": "and they are also easy for people to read: commits, pull requests, docs.",
          "start": 72.014,
          "end": 76.295
        },
        {
          "text": "The team even shares the same tools.",
          "start": 77.577,
          "end": 79.563
        },
        {
          "text": "Third, knowledge.",
          "start": 81.526,
          "end": 82.721
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia starts out knowing nothing about your work. It learns as you go.",
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 88.674
        },
        {
          "text": "It scans each project to understand how it is built,",
          "start": 89.915,
          "end": 93.189
        },
        {
          "text": "it keeps the decisions you have made,",
          "start": 94.057,
          "end": 95.89
        },
        {
          "text": "it remembers what was left open,",
          "start": 96.768,
          "end": 98.335
        },
        {
          "text": "and it saves every piece of work in a clear, structured way, so it can be found later.",
          "start": 99.158,
          "end": 103.99
        },
        {
          "text": "Fourth, being able to see where things stand.",
          "start": 106.256,
          "end": 108.697
        },
        {
          "text": "Every idea is written down, so it does not get lost in a chat.",
          "start": 110.026,
          "end": 113.326
        },
        {
          "text": "It becomes a plan,",
          "start": 114.494,
          "end": 115.62
        },
        {
          "text": "the plan becomes small tasks, and each task comes with its own test.",
          "start": 116.441,
          "end": 120.477
        },
        {
          "text": "At the end, a different agent checks the result, one that did not do the work.",
          "start": 121.69,
          "end": 126.452
        },
        {
          "text": "And fifth, audit: knowing who answers for what.",
          "start": 128.62,
          "end": 132.147
        },
        {
          "text": "When a change really matters, a person is in charge, and has to approve it.",
          "start": 133.309,
          "end": 137.417
        },
        {
          "text": "Every step leaves a trail you can follow,",
          "start": 138.619,
          "end": 140.712
        },
        {
          "text": "every piece of work gets a grade,",
          "start": 141.393,
          "end": 143.137
        },
        {
          "text": "and bad habits are flagged, so they can be fixed.",
          "start": 143.843,
          "end": 146.565
        },
        {
          "text": "Those five things are what Gaia brings to a team.",
          "start": 148.968,
          "end": 151.765
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, let's see how it does it.",
          "start": 152.882,
          "end": 154.428
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": "p2-the-map",
      "audio": "audio/2.wav",
      "duration": 152.68,
      "method": "sentences",
      "speech": [
        0.206,
        152.11
      ],
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Let's start with the question itself: what is Gaia?",
          "start": 0.206,
          "end": 3.121
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia is a layer that sits between you and your AI agents.",
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 8.107
        },
        {
          "text": "It talks with you and coordinates the work, but it never makes the changes itself.",
          "start": 9.251,
          "end": 13.388
        },
        {
          "text": "You only talk to one agent: the orchestrator. There is one per session.",
          "start": 14.512,
          "end": 18.989
        },
        {
          "text": "It listens to what you want, in your own words, and decides what has to happen.",
          "start": 20.133,
          "end": 24.397
        },
        {
          "text": "Before it starts, it shows you the route, so you can change it on the way.",
          "start": 25.787,
          "end": 29.889
        },
        {
          "text": "But the orchestrator never edits a file.",
          "start": 32.115,
          "end": 34.244
        },
        {
          "text": "It hands the work to a specialist, the agent that knows that field best.",
          "start": 35.569,
          "end": 39.702
        },
        {
          "text": "There are eight today: one for code, one for infrastructure, one for live systems, and more. You can add your own.",
          "start": 40.964,
          "end": 48.55
        },
        {
          "text": "Each one starts clean, for one piece of work. When it is done, it sends back a contract: a report in a fixed form.",
          "start": 49.943,
          "end": 57.004
        },
        {
          "text": "Starting clean does not mean starting empty.",
          "start": 59.373,
          "end": 61.794
        },
        {
          "text": "The moment a specialist starts, Gaia hands it five things.",
          "start": 62.953,
          "end": 66.508
        },
        {
          "text": "Its identity: what it is for, and what it may touch.",
          "start": 67.573,
          "end": 70.607
        },
        {
          "text": "Its skills: the team's way of doing that kind of work.",
          "start": 71.537,
          "end": 74.508
        },
        {
          "text": "The project context: what Gaia knows about the project, and which parts it may read or write.",
          "start": 75.372,
          "end": 81.21
        },
        {
          "text": "What Gaia knows about you: your rules and preferences, so it does not ask you again.",
          "start": 82.089,
          "end": 87.296
        },
        {
          "text": "And its contract, open from the start: the goal, and the form it has to fill in.",
          "start": 88.244,
          "end": 92.894
        },
        {
          "text": "While the work runs, rules in code keep watch.",
          "start": 95.21,
          "end": 98.416
        },
        {
          "text": "If a specialist needs to change something that matters, Gaia stops it and shows you the exact command, what it changes, and how to undo it.",
          "start": 99.477,
          "end": 107.847
        },
        {
          "text": "Nothing runs until you answer.",
          "start": 109.021,
          "end": 110.763
        },
        {
          "text": "And when the specialist reports back, its contract is checked before the orchestrator uses it for the next step.",
          "start": 112.148,
          "end": 118.131
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Gaia keeps what should outlive the session.",
          "start": 120.427,
          "end": 123.523
        },
        {
          "text": "The decisions you made and why, what was learned, the work still open, and how you like to work.",
          "start": 124.72,
          "end": 131.474
        },
        {
          "text": "Ideas become plans, and plans become tasks that another agent checks before they count as done.",
          "start": 132.829,
          "end": 138.749
        },
        {
          "text": "So the next session starts where this one ended.",
          "start": 140.355,
          "end": 142.609
        },
        {
          "text": "All of this runs through one tool: Gaia's own command line.",
          "start": 144.734,
          "end": 148.185
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, let's look closer at what Gaia knows.",
          "start": 149.269,
          "end": 152.11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": "p5-what-gaia-keeps",
      "audio": "audio/5.wav",
      "duration": 158.1,
      "method": "sentences",
      "speech": [
        0.212,
        157.645
      ],
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "What do you know about my work?",
          "start": 0.212,
          "end": 1.726
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia starts with nothing. Everything it knows, it learned while working with you.",
          "start": 2.868,
          "end": 7.693
        },
        {
          "text": "It keeps that in four memories, and each one answers a simple question.",
          "start": 9.048,
          "end": 12.854
        },
        {
          "text": "The first one asks: what do we know about the project, and about you?",
          "start": 14.909,
          "end": 18.797
        },
        {
          "text": "When you open a project, Gaia scans the workspace and its repositories, and writes down what it finds, section by section.",
          "start": 20.257,
          "end": 27.123
        },
        {
          "text": "Each specialist is told which of those sections it may read, and which it may write.",
          "start": 28.411,
          "end": 33.08
        },
        {
          "text": "It also keeps what is yours: your rules, your preferences, and the decisions you made, with the reason behind them.",
          "start": 34.304,
          "end": 41.053
        },
        {
          "text": "The second asks: what are we doing, and what is still open?",
          "start": 43.282,
          "end": 46.681
        },
        {
          "text": "Bigger work starts as a brief: a short page that says what you want, and how you will know it is done.",
          "start": 48.011,
          "end": 55.087
        },
        {
          "text": "The brief becomes one plan,",
          "start": 56.609,
          "end": 58.199
        },
        {
          "text": "and the plan is split into tasks. Each task carries its own checks, called gates.",
          "start": 59.057,
          "end": 64.218
        },
        {
          "text": "If the plan has to change, the change is recorded, and the earlier version is kept.",
          "start": 65.506,
          "end": 70.085
        },
        {
          "text": "And whatever is paused, blocked or pending carries forward to the next session.",
          "start": 71.213,
          "end": 75.479
        },
        {
          "text": "The third asks: what did we do, and what came out of it?",
          "start": 77.714,
          "end": 81.622
        },
        {
          "text": "Every turn ends with its contract: how it ended, and the evidence behind it.",
          "start": 83.116,
          "end": 87.761
        },
        {
          "text": "Every change you approved is kept, with your answer.",
          "start": 88.933,
          "end": 91.712
        },
        {
          "text": "And every check leaves its verdict: pass or fail, and what is still open.",
          "start": 93.067,
          "end": 97.383
        },
        {
          "text": "Together, they form an audit trail you can follow later.",
          "start": 98.685,
          "end": 101.434
        },
        {
          "text": "The fourth asks: what happened, and when?",
          "start": 103.463,
          "end": 106.051
        },
        {
          "text": "This one nobody writes. Gaia's engine records it on its own, as events, turns and sessions.",
          "start": 107.476,
          "end": 113.863
        },
        {
          "text": "Put in order, they become a timeline.",
          "start": 115.055,
          "end": 117.074
        },
        {
          "text": "Anything unusual is flagged, and a turn that was cut short is marked, so nothing disappears quietly.",
          "start": 118.442,
          "end": 124.355
        },
        {
          "text": "And each new session starts with the last twenty-four hours.",
          "start": 125.712,
          "end": 129.613
        },
        {
          "text": "These four memories are not separate boxes.",
          "start": 131.743,
          "end": 133.951
        },
        {
          "text": "A single task leaves a trace in all four: in the project it touched, in the plan it belongs to, in its contract, and in the record of its turn.",
          "start": 135.211,
          "end": 144.942
        },
        {
          "text": "You decide what is worth keeping. The engine records the rest.",
          "start": 147.634,
          "end": 151.733
        },
        {
          "text": "But knowing is not enough. What happens when the work needs to change something?",
          "start": 152.906,
          "end": 157.645
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": "p-pilot-your-yes",
      "audio": "audio/7.wav",
      "duration": 93.96,
      "method": "sentences",
      "speech": [
        0.207,
        93.494
      ],
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Let's follow one request, from your question to the result.",
          "start": 0.207,
          "end": 3.345
        },
        {
          "text": "It starts with you: you ask for something, in your own words.",
          "start": 5.128,
          "end": 8.927
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, the orchestrator, the agent you talk to, sends the job to a specialist.",
          "start": 9.872,
          "end": 14.542
        },
        {
          "text": "Before it starts, Gaia gives it what it needs: the goal, your rules, and a form to fill in.",
          "start": 15.493,
          "end": 21.921
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the specialist does the work.",
          "start": 23.617,
          "end": 25.585
        },
        {
          "text": "It reads files, edits code, and runs tests.",
          "start": 26.555,
          "end": 29.85
        },
        {
          "text": "All the while, Gaia checks every action with fixed rules.",
          "start": 31.185,
          "end": 34.647
        },
        {
          "text": "Safe actions go through, so you are not asked.",
          "start": 35.722,
          "end": 38.784
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the specialist wants to push the code.",
          "start": 40.553,
          "end": 42.985
        },
        {
          "text": "That changes something other people use.",
          "start": 43.994,
          "end": 46.46
        },
        {
          "text": "So Gaia stops it, and the specialist waits.",
          "start": 47.468,
          "end": 50.17
        },
        {
          "text": "This is where you come in: the orchestrator asks you.",
          "start": 51.792,
          "end": 54.754
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia writes the question, and checks it word for word.",
          "start": 56.531,
          "end": 59.545
        },
        {
          "text": "You see who asks, the exact command, and how to undo it.",
          "start": 60.556,
          "end": 64.321
        },
        {
          "text": "Let's say you approve.",
          "start": 66.397,
          "end": 67.552
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia writes down your answer.",
          "start": 68.487,
          "end": 69.84
        },
        {
          "text": "It works once, for this command only.",
          "start": 71.059,
          "end": 73.341
        },
        {
          "text": "With that, the specialist continues where it stopped.",
          "start": 74.402,
          "end": 77.42
        },
        {
          "text": "The command runs, exactly as you approved it.",
          "start": 79.061,
          "end": 81.983
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaia checks the specialist's report.",
          "start": 82.87,
          "end": 84.972
        },
        {
          "text": "And only then does the orchestrator tell you the result.",
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 88.74
        },
        {
          "text": "Nothing that matters runs without you seeing it.",
          "start": 90.665,
          "end": 93.494
        }
      ]
    },
